---
description: Do not push or open a PR unless asked. One PR per issue. Update an open PR instead of opening another.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Pull requests

- Do not push or open a pull request unless the user explicitly asks.
- Create only one PR per session/issue unless told otherwise.
- If a PR already exists for the issue, add commits to it. Do not open another PR for the same work.
- Keep the original PR title and purpose. Update the description only when needed.
- Before pushing to an existing PR branch, check that the PR is still open. If it was closed or merged, create a new branch and a new PR instead of pushing to the old one.
